* MiCA\nRegulation (EU) 2023/1114
** Object (Art. 1)
*** Disclosure: crypto-asset white paper
*** Authorisation of CASPs, ART and EMT issuers
*** Protection of holders and clients
*** Market integrity
** Scope (Art. 2)
*** Activities in the Union
*** Excluded persons: intra-group, central banks, EIB, ESM
*** Excluded assets
**** Financial instruments (MiFID II)
**** Deposits, funds, insurance, pensions
**** Unique, non-fungible tokens
** Three categories (Art. 3)
*** E-money token: one official currency
*** Asset-referenced token: other value or basket
*** Other crypto-assets
**** Utility tokens
** Actors
*** Offeror / issuer / person seeking admission
*** Crypto-asset service provider (10 services)
*** Retail holder, client
*** Competent authority, home and host Member State
*** EBA and ESMA
** Structure
*** Title II: white paper
*** Titles III–IV: stablecoins
*** Title V: CASPs
*** Titles VI–VII: market abuse, supervision
*** Annexes I–VI
** Timeline
*** 29 June 2023: entry into force
*** 30 June 2024: Titles III and IV
*** 30 December 2024: all other titles
*** 1 July 2026: end of CASP transition
*** 31 December 2027: white papers for old listings
*** 10 January 2030: ESAP
